alfe-open-relative-path-not-resolved-vs-cwd — (open "rel/path" ...) fails via alfe, works in clautolisp
======================================================================================================

*** RESOLVED in alfe 1.7.23. ***
`alfe --clautolisp` now resolves cwd-relative paths, matching direct
clautolisp: from the repo `(open "src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r")` => handle;
a bogus relative name => NIL; the same call from cwd=/tmp => NIL. No
difference between alfe and direct clautolisp remains.

Reported from: SCHMS+ loader generation (dev/lisp/make-loader.lsp) run
headless. clautolisp 1.7.x / alfe 1.7.3 (broken) -> 1.7.23 (fixed).

*** Attribution corrected: this is an ALFE bug, not clautolisp. ***
clautolisp invoked directly resolves cwd-relative paths correctly;
only the `alfe --clautolisp` front-end fails to.

Symptom
-------

`(open "src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r")` — a path RELATIVE to the process
current working directory — returns NIL under `alfe --clautolisp`, even
though the file exists and the process cwd is the repo root. The same
expression opens the file when clautolisp is invoked DIRECTLY, and
BricsCAD/AutoCAD also resolve it against the current directory.

Repro (cwd = a dir containing src-vlx/schmsplus.prj)
---------------------------------------------------

    clautolisp --no-init --dialect clautolisp --host mock \
      -x '(princ (if (open "src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r") "OK" "NIL"))'
    => OK          # direct clautolisp: relative path resolved

    alfe --no-init --clautolisp --host mock \
      -x '(princ (if (open "src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r") "OK" "NIL"))'
    => NIL         # via alfe: relative path NOT resolved

    alfe --no-init --clautolisp --host mock \
      -x '(princ (if (open "<abs>/src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r") "OK" "NIL"))'
    => OK          # via alfe: absolute path works

TRUSTEDPATHS makes no difference (not a SECURELOAD gate).

Diagnosis
---------

Since direct clautolisp succeeds and only `alfe --clautolisp` fails,
alfe must run the hosted engine with a different working directory (or
resolve relative filenames against a different base — e.g. its install
dir or a temp dir) than the process cwd. alfe should resolve
cwd-relative filenames against the invoking process's current directory,
matching direct clautolisp and BricsCAD/AutoCAD.

Impact
------

SCHMS+ generates `schmsplus-loader.lsp` (the clautolisp equivalent of
the `.vlx`/`.des` CAD artifacts) with a headless AutoLISP tool. Using
`clautolisp` DIRECTLY (the intended invocation for such tool use) avoids
the problem entirely and needs no absolute paths, so the loader's
embedded default directory stays relative/portable. This bug only bites
callers who go through `alfe --clautolisp`; fixing it would let either
entry point be used interchangeably for headless file tooling.

Related: cad-path-dotdot-resolution.issue,
cad-vl-filename-directory-and-load.issue.
